        "raw": "<p>I&#39;d also suggest keeping the updates on the &#39;Updates&#39; page. The first real information on the Campaign page is the post about Silhouette, which entirely fails to introduce your premise or setting, and makes a bunch of references to things we don&#39;t know yet, because we&#39;ve just got here and have no idea what&#39;s going on. It is unreasonably difficult to find what your books are actually&nbsp;<em>about</em>, and why we should care about them. That info needs to be front and centre.</p><p>EDIT: I just watched some of your campaign video; you don&#39;t even really introduce the comics until two minutes in. The campaign video is your hard sell, and you need to take advantage of that. To compare to another comics project:&nbsp;https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/sonson/kuruz-volume-2-one-by-one?ref=category_recommended - I watched 30 seconds of this campaign video and I now know what the premise of the guy&#39;s comic is and have seen some of the art to boot. People have short attention spans, and you need to hook them sharpish.</p>",
