      {
        "id": 149878,
        "name": "oddthomas",
        "username": "oddthomas",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/o/58956e/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-10-25T08:27:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey guys! Thanks for the feedback. I really&nbsp;appreciate it. Even though this kick starter may fail its okay. I learned alot and thanks to you guys I learned even more. Sometimes you have to fail to succeed, but the only way to do that is find how why and how you failed. You guys helped with that. If I do another kick start campaign I'll take what you guys said and apply it to the next one.&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Spiff I think you were spot on when you said I need to sell it better, and I think that goes in to what meerkat was saying as well. The video should have been done alot &nbsp;better. It was probably the weakest part of the kick start, when it should have been the strongest. Silver Leaf you are right about the shipping and the confidence of the costumer. Just because I think Ia have a great product diesnt mean people wknow that and back it. They need to have confidence in me managing the project. Really good feedback. Thank you.&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 5,
